course: dictionary
lesson: 7548
title: Preference: what you like best
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A preference is a liking for one thing more than another. If you like apples more than pears, you have a preference for apples. The word comes from prefer, which means to like one thing better.
explain: «In Australia, voters number the candidates in order of preference.» Here the order runs from first choice to last choice. A voter writes 1 next to their first choice, 2 next to their second, and so on.
explain: «He blushed for pleasure at the old seaman's commendations.» Commendations means praise, so the seaman was giving praise and the man felt happy about it. Preference can also mean treating one person or group first, as in «give preference to».
explain: A preference like «I have a preference for blue» is fine without proof, because it is about what you like. Saying something IS better needs reasons that other people can check and share.
fact: A preference is a liking for one thing more than another.
fact: The thing you like more, or choose, is also called your preference.
fact: «Give preference to» means treat someone first or better.
fact: Useful phrases: «a preference for», «in order of preference», «personal preference».
fact: In maths, a survey of preferences, such as favourite fruit, can be shown in a bar chart or a tally chart.
exercise: In a class survey, 12 children had a preference for apples and 8 for bananas. Which fruit did more children prefer? | *Apples | Bananas | They were equal | Neither fruit
exercise: «Voters number the candidates in order of preference.» What does in order of preference mean? | In any random mix | *From first choice to last choice | By age, youngest first | Alphabetically, from A to Z
exercise: What does «give preference to» mean? | Ignore someone completely | Give someone a present | Ask someone a question | *Treat someone first or better
test: In «blushed for pleasure at the old seaman's commendations», what do commendations mean? | *Praise | Questions | Insults | Storms
test: Which sentence is a personal preference? | Blue is the best colour, and everyone must agree. | *I have a preference for blue. | Blue is worse than red for every reason. | Red is better than blue because it is louder.
exam: Which statement needs reasons that others can share? | My favourite pet is a dog | *Dogs are better than cats | I like cats more than dogs | I have a preference for dogs
